# Open-Locker Monorepo Architecture

Open-Locker is an API-first IoT monorepo.

## Components

- `locker-backend/`: Laravel 12 REST API and Filament 5 admin panel. It owns
  authentication, domain state, event sourcing, MQTT publication, and the
  Scramble OpenAPI document.
- `mobile-app/`: React Native/Expo client. It consumes generated TypeScript RTK
  Query hooks.
- `locker-client/`: TypeScript service deployed on a Raspberry Pi. It bridges
  MQTT commands to serialized Modbus RTU operations.
- `docs/`: Architecture documentation and ADRs.

## Boundaries

`Mobile app -> Laravel API -> MQTT -> locker-client -> Modbus RTU -> hardware`

- The backend does not communicate with Modbus hardware directly.
- The mobile app does not hand-maintain API types.
- The admin panel is the only server-rendered UI.
- Mosquitto authenticates through the backend's `/api/mosq/*` endpoints.

## API generation

- Scramble serves the current OpenAPI document at `/docs/api.json`; do not rely
  on a committed export.
- From `mobile-app/`, run `pnpm run generate:api` while the backend is reachable
  at `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL`.
- Update mobile consumers after regeneration. Never hand-edit
  `src/store/generatedApi.ts`.

For cross-component contract or architecture changes, follow the ADR rules in
`.cursor/rules/general/`.
